============================================================================
CSL fork scope
============================================================================

The "CSL fork" copyright above covers only the modifications made by
CSL Tech Solutions to the Ararat Synapse sources — specifically:

- ldapsend.pas V1.7.x: tri-platform POSIX support (6 SSPI blocks under
  IFDEF MSWINDOWS + POSIX stubs for BindGSSAPI/SignLDAPMessage/
  VerifyLDAPMessage); automatic LDAP attribute typing (TLDAPValueType
  enum + ~110 AD attributes static map + TLDAPAttributeValue record);
  AddRaw(AnsiString) bypassing AnsiString->UnicodeString implicit
  conversion in the ASN.1 parser.
- blcksock.pas: GetPeerCertSHA256Hash for RFC 5929 Channel Binding Token.
- synautil.pas: FileTime AD helpers.
- ssl_openssl4.pas / ssl_openssl4_lib.pas: OpenSSL 4.0 support (100% new,
  mechanical fork of ssl_openssl3).
- ssl_openssl_paths.pas: TOpenSSLPaths.Apply(N) / SetDllDirectory helper.
- jedi.inc: full rewrite (~4350 lines).
- synacode.pas, synaip.pas, synafpc.pas: minor patches.

The original upstream Ararat Synapse codebase remains the copyright of
Lukas Gebauer. Contact: <https://www.ararat.cz/synapse/>
Fork base: <https://github.com/geby/synapse>
